From: Arctic Linux maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Destroy scene output before changing layer surfaces

The retained BIOS ISO diagnostic aborts in wlr_output_finish during a VT
switch. Destroying layer scene nodes while this output is still active can
create a surface-enter bind listener which misses the destroy signal being
emitted. Remove the scene output before any layer or lock teardown.

Related upstream analysis and fix:
https://github.com/labwc/labwc/pull/3701
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wlroots/wlroots/-/issues/4096

--- a/src/manage/monitor.c
+++ b/src/manage/monitor.c
@@ -836,6 +836,12 @@
 
 	m->iscleanuping = true;
 
+	/* Stop surface-enter callbacks for the dying output before layer/lock
+	 * teardown changes the scene. New bind listeners would otherwise miss
+	 * the destroy signal in progress and make wlr_output_finish abort. */
+	wlr_scene_output_destroy(m->scene_output);
+	m->scene_output = NULL;
+
 	/* m->layers[i] are intentionally not unlinked */
 	for (i = 0; i < LENGTH(m->layers); i++) {
 		wl_list_for_each_safe(l, tmp, &m->layers[i], link)
@@ -855,7 +861,6 @@
 		handle_session_lock_surface_destroy(&m->destroy_lock_surface, NULL);
 	m->wlr_output->data = NULL;
 
-	wlr_scene_output_destroy(m->scene_output);
 	wlr_output_layout_remove(server.output_layout, m->wlr_output);
 
 	monitor_close(m);
